    "sceneBrief": "At daybreak, Rainsford is awakened by the baying of hounds. Zaroff has released the whole pack. Rainsford knows the end is near. Fleeing through the jungle, he remembers a native trick from Uganda: he bends a springy sapling, ties his hunting knife to it with wild grapevine, blade pointing down the trail, and releases the tension. He runs. The baying grows closer. When it stops abruptly, Rainsford climbs a tree and looks back. General Zaroff is still standing — but Ivan lies dead, the knife having found his heart. Rainsford is now unarmed, and the hounds pick up the cry again.",
